    {
      "id": 84570,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-12-24T19:35:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I added an Extreme category for ones I've done, but are harder than the normal hard ones.</p><p>Easy:</p><p>Unload!: &nbsp;Fire all five of Expat's guns in one Unload.</p><p>Medium:</p><p>Praise God and Pass the Ammunition: &nbsp;Use four or more Ammo cards in one turn. &nbsp;</p><p><span>I'm No Villain (character card): &nbsp;Have the Operative destroy the Chairman</span></p><p>Hard:</p><p><span>Full Assault: &nbsp;Use all Six of Expat's Weapons (Guns+RPG Launcher) on someone else's turn.</span></p><p><span>Safety Week: &nbsp;Defeat Plague Rat in Pike Industrial Complex without heroes destroying an environment card.</span></p><p><span>Slight of Hand: &nbsp;As Argent Adept have other heroes play 5 cards during your turn.</span></p><p><span>EXTREME!!!</span></p><p>No Animals were Harmed: &nbsp;Defeat the Matriarch when no hero target deals damage to a fowl card. &nbsp;</p><p><span>Flower Power: &nbsp;Defeat Akash'bhuta when no hero target but The Argent Adept deals damage to a villain target.</span></p><div>&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The three Expat challenges I pulled off at once, vs. Akash. &nbsp;Expat ended up Lowest HP and stayed there for 5 rounds while three different brambles pinned me down. &nbsp;My friends didn't seem too worried about it, with Speed Loading and Load putting cards in play and Salvage Yard and TLT feeding me cards I was well prepared. &nbsp;As soon as the brambles were gone Adept let me play Unload, I had all 5 guns, RPG Launcher in hand and 6 ammo cards in play. &nbsp;It was nice.</div><p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 11,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:07:58.750Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
